# Coding Standards (Permanent)

## General

- Write code for the next engineer: obvious names, small functions, explicit errors.
- No commented-out dead code. No unused imports.
- Avoid premature abstraction; extract when a pattern repeats **twice** with clear stability.
- Every tenant-owned row/document: `businessId` required + indexed; queries always constrained.
- Timestamps everywhere meaningful; soft-delete only where product needs restore — never soft-delete payment ledgers.

## NestJS (API)

- Strict TypeScript. Explicit DTO classes + `class-validator` (or Zod pipes) on inputs.
- Use Enums for statuses (`SubscriptionStatus`, etc.).
- Authorization: JWT AuthGuard + Business membership + EntitlementGuard.
- Side effects (SMS, payment, PDF) via **BullMQ/Redis** jobs; HTTP handlers stay fast.
- Domain exceptions mapped through a global filter to `{ code, message }` JSON.
- PostgreSQL: no unbounded `findMany` on tenant tables — paginate.
- MongoDB: always filter `businessId`; validate payload against `document-schema`.
- Storage paths via config — never hardcode OS paths.

```typescript
// ✅ Gate then act
await this.entitlements.assertCan(businessId, 'export.pdf');
await this.exportQueue.add('pdf', { documentId });
```

## Next.js (Web)

- App Router + TypeScript strict. No `any` unless justified with a short comment.
- Server Components by default; Client Components only when interactivity requires.
- User-facing copy via i18n (`fa`/`en`); colors via theme tokens (dark/light).
- Call Nest through `shared/api`; do not scatter raw `fetch` with duplicated auth headers.
- Entitlements: read from API; disable UI; never trust UI-only checks.
- Editor state: client store with undo/redo + debounced autosave to API.

```tsx
// ✅ Feature hook + shared API
const { data } = useBusinessDocuments(businessId);
```

## Shared packages

- Document JSON changes go in `packages/document-schema` first, then Nest + Next consumers.
- Breaking schema changes: version bump + note in `docs/`.

## Tests (minimum bar)

- Services with money/trial/entitlements: unit/e2e tests.
- Critical HTTP: OTP happy-path + rate limit; subscription gate deny.
- Do not merge billing or gate changes without tests.
